            <div xml:id="d998">

                <pb facs="0910" n="806" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg806"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.51/79.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-06-02T21:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 2, 1913—9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>266. Mexican loan of 200,000,000 pesos has been definitely concluded. Speyer
                    Brothers share in this loan as creditors and also directly through their
                    European houses.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Lane Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
